13:["$","section",null,{"className":"section section-foam theme-light","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":["$","div",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":"920px"},"children":[["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"2.2rem","marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":"The geological thesis: Atlantic margin Cretaceous fans"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"lede","style":{"color":"var(--muted)","marginBottom":"1.8rem"},"children":"Over the past two decades, deepwater basin floor fan plays have emerged as the most prolific hydrocarbon exploration target along Africa’s Atlantic margin."}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The geological success story along the transform margin is anchored by major benchmark discoveries: from the multi-billion-barrel ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Jubilee discovery in Ghana"}]," (which first established the Cretaceous turbidite fan model along the margin), to the giant ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Baleine and Calao discoveries offshore Côte d'Ivoire"}]," immediately adjacent to Liberia, and the unprecedented ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Venus light-oil discovery in the Orange Basin offshore Namibia"}],"."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The Harper Basin shares the same regional Cretaceous syn-rift to post-rift depositional dynamics, robust Cenomanian-Turonian marine source kitchens, and steep slope channels feeding high-net-to-gross basin floor fans. With seven major fan systems already identified on regional 3D seismic, BluEnergies and TotalEnergies are applying modern reprocessing and seabed geochemical mapping to de-risk drilling targets in this undrilled frontier."}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"36px","display":"flex","gap":"16px","flexWrap":"wrap"},"children":[["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/assets-and-operations/overview/","className":"btn btn-primary","children":"Explore the asset"}],["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/investors/presentations/","className":"btn btn-secondary btn-secondary-light","children":"Download corporate pre